{
  "name": "First Client - Production Send Executor - Control Center",
  "active": true,
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "Listmonk API\n\nConfigured through n8n environment variables."
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -448,
        272
      ],
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "id": "55968e07-9e68-41e7-9dd7-22cf7a58fc7b",
      "name": "Sticky Note"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "PRODUCTION SETUP\n\nRequired n8n environment variables:\n1. LISTMONK_API_BASIC = current Listmonk Authorization value.\n2. LISTMONK_TX_TEMPLATE_ID = Listmonk transactional template ID.\n3. FIRST_CLIENT_CAMPAIGN_ID = campaign ID to execute.\n4. FIRST_CLIENT_SEND_MODE = real or disabled. Keep disabled until the controlled test passes.\n5. FIRST_CLIENT_STALE_MINUTES = stale-send recovery threshold, normally 30.\n\nProduction rules:\n- PostgreSQL is the source of truth.\n- The worker claims exactly one recipient per execution.\n- The real-send safety gate runs before a recipient is claimed.\n- Never hard-code API credentials or campaign/template IDs in this workflow.\n- Verify PostgreSQL rate-limit and retry-backoff enforcement before activation.\n- Provider/event reconciliation and unsubscribe/bounce/complaint synchronization remain separate production workflows.\n\n\n### FINAL PRODUCTION HARDENING\n- Environment values are read from container env vars.\n- Real-send gate reads Production Send Configuration directly.\n- Provider success accepts Listmonk response in either top-level or body.data.\n- Success finalization uses mark_send_success_production, which does not double-count rate usage because claim_one_send_slot reserves the slot.\n- Keep workflow inactive until the controlled real-send test passes.\n",
        "height": 260,
        "width": 420
      },
      "id": "71fd52dd-9e4e-4ac1-a6bb-91854acf2fb8",
      "name": "Production Setup Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        0,
        96
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "DATABASE PREREQUISITES BEFORE PRODUCTION\n\n1. claim_one_send_slot must enforce campaign/global rate limits.\n2. claim_one_send_slot must exclude queued recipients whose latest retry has next_retry_at > NOW().\n3. Stale recovery must only recover sends after the configured threshold.\n4. Provider acceptance followed by worker crash is an inherent delivery ambiguity. Keep recipient='sending' until stale recovery, and reconcile provider events separately.\n5. Keep the separate provider-event/unsubscribe/bounce reconciliation workflow in production.",
        "height": 250,
        "width": 420
      },
      "id": "b35bbc8e-a6d9-4f23-8cd4-ea026373414f",
      "name": "Database Production Prerequisites",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        704,
        304
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "LISTMONK API SECURITY\n\nDo not store API tokens in workflow nodes or sticky notes.\nUse n8n environment variable LISTMONK_API_BASIC.\nRotate any credential that has previously been exposed.\n"
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        640,
        112
      ],
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "id": "6c6faea2-7438-453c-86b2-5b44df36f5b1",
      "name": "Sticky Note1"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "PRODUCTION SEND EXECUTOR\n\nPurpose\n• One controlled email-send attempt per workflow execution.\n• PostgreSQL is the source of truth.\n• Listmonk is the transactional delivery engine.\n• The workflow never chooses recipients directly.\n\nControl flow\n1. Configuration validation\n2. Recover stale sends\n3. Activate due campaign\n4. Confirm campaign is running\n5. REAL-SEND SAFETY GATE\n6. Claim exactly one send slot\n7. Create send attempt\n8. Load + validate send context\n9. Send through Listmonk\n10. Record success/failure\n11. Finalize campaign if complete\n\nCRITICAL\nThe real-send gate is BEFORE recipient claim.\nThere is only ONE path into the gate.\nThis prevents duplicate claims in a single execution.",
        "height": 310,
        "width": 600
      },
      "id": "255f53be-2f74-4ef9-864b-737137516ef0",
      "name": "01 • EXECUTOR ARCHITECTURE",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        1184,
        208
      ]
    },
